id: core/movement-frame
title: "movement frame"
kind: core
status: v1
updated: 2026-07-21

definition: >
  A movement frame is the movement layer inside an orientation shape. It turns
  raw signal into an attributed state snapshot, scoped possibilities or
  targets, a typed lacuna, bounded transition intent, proof, and an authorized
  state update.

path:
  - signal
  - orientation
  - choice
  - move
  - proof
  - update

fields:
  current: "an attributed snapshot of what is happening now"
  possible: "a possibility, not automatically a target"
  desire: "a principal's attributed directional evidence"
  target: "an optional scoped condition with ratification rights"
  lacuna: "a typed inadequacy relative to a target, requirement, question, boundary, or proof condition"
  move: "an authorized transition attempt that cannot prove itself"
  boundary: "what must not be forced"
  proof: "what would update the map"
  update: "the authorized event reduction after proof and world response"
  replay: "the deterministic reconstruction of state and what changed"

compatibility:
  frame.current: "read as an attributed state snapshot"
  frame.possible: "read as a possibility or target candidate according to context"
  possible_kind_desired: "read as a desire plus proposed attain-target, never a ratified goal"

proof:
  source:
    - readme.yawn
    - core/movement-loop.yawn
  status: seed-backed
